$(1,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470405} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af74279b-63b5-5d79-8259-57fc9b29a647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469588} {:answer/id #uuid "422d0615-7052-5247-8065-184d37fec22e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "422d0615-7052-5247-8065-184d37fec22e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469589} :answer-field/id #uuid "c39184ad-8688-52c6-80fc-34cdcfa71132" :answer-field/key "The point $(5,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da6f4133-24dc-5140-aaa0-0ea075dfe3f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-9255" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(3,2),(14,6),$ and $(9,2).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2-0}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(-1,1),(2,3),(5,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The point $(5,1)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357523 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertices of a Polygon Given Its Image Under a Linear Transformation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049213 :topic/id #uuid "e3ec8239-fcb5-5753-aa06-6c1a1dcb3ccb" :topic/math-academy-id 988 :topic/title "Inverting Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c350a3-1b79-58a9-a807-6ab58e5c39d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469590} {:answer/id #uuid "459d147b-5230-51a3-b435-5764d57b48f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51c350a3-1b79-58a9-a807-6ab58e5c39d1" :answer/type 