lty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1174578d-6631-5fcf-81bf-729c1fac3da6" :question/math-academy-id "q-9258" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(4,-1),(17,-3),$ and $(10,-1).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-1-0}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(-1,1),(2,3),(5,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The point $(-1,1)$”; “The point $(5,1)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertices of a Polygon Given Its Image Under a Linear Transformation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049213 :topic/id #uuid "e3ec8239-fcb5-5753-aa06-6c1a1dcb3ccb" :topic/math-academy-id 988 :topic/title "Inverting Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77b25b30-e0bb-5259-9539-cf0d164d3467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469596} {:answer/id #uuid "eabf8157-2e6a-5210-bbcc-06fd9c4f3272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eabf8157-2e6a-5210-bbcc-06fd9c4f3272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469597} :answer-field/id #uuid "28ae18bd-3280-53d5-9fcd-448d879f7c0a" :answer-field/key "The point $(0,-3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470410} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8cf7fa1-e149-501b-b2e3-3ed65df17e23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469598} {:answer/id #uuid "f7782d42-4cf1-52c7-89d6-678892697267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8cf7fa1-e149-501b-b2e3-3ed65df17e23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469598} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb5831cf-9d5a-55f3-87f8-440f5b3f12f1" :answer-field/key "The point $(3,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470411} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "943d2282-2316-5feb-80f1-ef274b9b6334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469600} {:answer/id #uuid "ea36bc5d-0f0b-5664-ad09-08540fc57ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "943d2282-2316-5feb-80f1-ef274b9b6334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469600} :answer-field/id #uuid "4eccf71b-1fb1-55b0-9102-1181a0c2354c" :answer-field/key "The point $(-3,3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5f585952-0c84-59bf-89fe-d6813830d204" :question/math-academy-id "q-9260" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(-21,0),(21,0),$ and $(0,3).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-7-0}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -21\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(-3,0),(3,0),(0,-3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The point $(0,-3)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357525 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertices of a Polygon Given Its Image Under a Linear Transformation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049213 :topic/id #uuid "e3ec8239-fcb5-5753-aa06-6c1a1dcb3ccb" :topic/math-academy-id 988 :topic/title "Inverting Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2157482-a1ed-5c32-91c2-2cab3e0b29c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469602} {:answer/id #uuid "08825dbb-0967-5083-b253-6d569886e119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2157482-a1ed-5c32-