7592186470415}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a755a352-feaa-5539-8e01-5e0ad683e5ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-9261" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(-2,2),(-5,4),(-3,2),$ and $(0,0).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3-2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,2),(-1,2),(-1,0),(0,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The point $(0,0)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357526 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertices of a Polygon Given Its Image Under a Linear Transformation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049213 :topic/id #uuid "e3ec8239-fcb5-5753-aa06-6c1a1dcb3ccb" :topic/math-academy-id 988 :topic/title "Inverting Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3307adb3-5e7b-5a1c-b154-e424b9a8cce4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469608} {:answer/id #uuid "16e994d5-8aca-50cd-b782-685a035d4e61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3307adb3-5e7b-5a1c-b154-e424b9a8cce4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469608} :answer-field/id #uuid "98432bd3-be83-56c5-be17-ef5c3526b650" :answer-field/key "The point $(1,3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470416} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a490851-61ea-542d-9ec2-ecbc61f04dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469610} {:answer/id #uuid "11d75742-d0ed-5b85-9531-f012f15d5ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11d75742-d0ed-5b85-9531-f012f15d5ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469611} :answer-field/id #uuid "20415130-a9ec-526d-b11a-edbb061373d9" :answer-field/key "The point $(3,3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470417} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86da18ef-3371-5b27-a2a4-337b78b73d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469612} {:answer/id #uuid "ac7dfe73-a4ed-57e1-b5f5-9ef81bfa244a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac7dfe73-a4ed-57e1-b5f5-9ef81bfa244a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469613} :answer-field/id #uuid "86423d97-11b1-595d-bf1a-f3d303cc250d" :answer-field/key "The point $(2,3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470418}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c32a27cb-e2ec-5eaa-a1cb-1ea5655b2b83" :question/math-academy-id "q-9262" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(2,-5),(3,-6),(4,-8),$ and $(3,-7).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0-1}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(1,2),(3,3),(4,4),(2,3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The point $(3,3)$”; “The point $(2,3)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357527 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertices of a Polygon Given Its Image Under a Linear Transformation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049213 :topic/id #uuid "e3ec8239-fcb5-5753-aa06-6c1a1dcb3ccb" :topic/math-academy-id 988 :topic/title "Inverting Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cb8c9e9-6518-56b3-b761-1900dbfdc0ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469614} {:answer/id #uuid "bd8782ff-f906-5f86-a2a5-645db754ee25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cb8c9e9-6518-56b3-b