 :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451959} {:answer/id #uuid "770810e2-9b98-501c-b7d6-38738d90eb12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b135c823-a7f2-5267-92f0-2062c99ce9db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451959} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5a8139b-28d0-5f8e-be9a-7298bbcbb11c" :answer-field/key "$E$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ffc0d2e-16d3-51e9-8958-0f5807298d55" :question/math-academy-id "q-94624" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$ and its subset $E$ containing all diagonal $2\\times 2$ matrices.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$E$ is closed under matrix addition” is true. If ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ are two matrices from $E,$ then \n\n$$\n{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}\n$$\n\n is a diagonal matrix. This matrix belongs to $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement “$E$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is true. If $A$ is an element of $E,$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\nkA\n$$\n\n is a diagonal matrix. This matrix belongs to $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$E$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is true, while statement “$E$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is false. $E$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$E$ is closed under matrix addition”; “$E$ is closed under scalar multiplication”; “$E$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "795fc022-fb5b-5f27-a5d8-aa4c2ad9dca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451961} {:answer/id #uuid "566a3a56-16f1-5b90-bea1-2f3ee57bb51e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "795fc022-fb5b-5f27-a5d8-aa4c2ad9dca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451961} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0f4fd63-51fe-513d-929c-04e865c20a46" :answer-field/key "$B$ is closed under matrix addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452828} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39e01aaf-2818-586e-bb60-43cf7bd3de14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451963} {:answer/id #uuid "e083d6c2-56a6-577a-92e4-6ba01e342ee7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39e01aaf-2818-586e-bb60-43cf7bd3de14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451963} :answer-field/id #uuid "5913234f-6a30-58d7-aabd-166bad7da71b" :answer-field/key "$B$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452829} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82e2ad3e-07c9-5fb2-9b3d-fe00002b1fb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451965} {:answer/id #uuid "40263c7a-0627-5200-bf3d-c2777958353f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82e2ad3e-07c9-5fb2-9b3d-fe00002b1fb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451965} :answer-field/id #uuid "963e43d6-331a-56e1-be82-da9c3690ac1f" :answer-field/key "$B$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452830} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18189e21-c99c-5d19-a3a8-4e8060b0797b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451967} {:answer/id #uuid "e6eb60f2-98a4-5b24-a94e-92f9324e2a78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6eb60f2-98a4-5b24-a94e-92f9324e2a78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451968} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bfdc7e3-3ad3-5cba-9513-6068b167a525" :answer-field/key "$B$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32515201-cdee-5802-875e-aaeaf04119b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-94625" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $B={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & a \\\\ 1-a & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a\\in R}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$B$ is closed under matrix addition” is false. For example, if ${A}_{1}={A}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a matrix from $B.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement “$B$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. For example, if $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $k=2,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =2\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a matrix from $B.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$B$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is false, while statement “$B$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is true. $B$ is a *not* subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$B$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"} :activity/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481565} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481747}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360463 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aae56ac2-5bb1-569e-a2cf-39b36f1898be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451969} {:answer/id #uuid "8f341029-5f9e-5f51-aa0f-790d336b421f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f341029-5f9e-5f51-aa0f-790d336b421f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451970} :answer-field/id #uuid "f45f2a09-7399-52cf-8200-6b78591e877e" :answer-field/key "$F$ is closed under matrix addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452832} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd6ebf9b-ae31-5d29-88c1-3f8598dba550" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451971} {:answer/id #uuid "555a1bc5-705d-5db1-9773-68d3374f6595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555a1bc5-705d-5db1-9773-68d3374f6595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451972} :answer-field/id #uuid "14b008ad-0fb6-5613-b50e-92e2b58c83d2" :answer-field/key "$F$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec6ff086-785f-53bc-b457-6b2b31c4589a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451973} {:answer/id #uuid "56af8a55-15fd-56c7-abed-495f3ed21ecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56af8a55-15fd-56c7-abed-495f3ed21ecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451974} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d352092-55c6-5249-8610-e3d700d0714a" :answer-field/key "$F$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "209355be-4c6a-5b2d-9589-305ac3e94a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451975} {:answer/id #uuid "06f65edf-35fd-5fc1-af4e-2cf290683638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "209355be-4c6a-5b2d-9589-305ac3e94a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451975} :answer-field/id #uuid "7baf2301-cbf3-56d6-89d2-5eacf3725845" :answer-field/key "$F$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c523e99-06d7-537c-99b6-2e21ff3e81b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-94629" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $F={A\\in {\\text{M}}_{2}(R)\\,|\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}A=A\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is closed under matrix addition” is true. If ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ are two matrices from $F,$ then ${A}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}{A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}{A}_{2}.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}_{1}+{A}_{2})\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & ={A}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}+{A}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}{A}_{1}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}{A}_{2} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}({A}_{1}+{A}_{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${A}_{1}+{A}_{2}$ is a matrix from $F.$ So, $F$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is true. If $A$ is an element of $F,$ then $A\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}A.$ For $k\\in R,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kA)\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & =k\\cdot A\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}(kA).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $kA$ is a matrix from $F.$ So, $F$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is true, while statement “$F$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is false. $F$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$F$ is closed under matrix addition”; “$F$ is closed under scalar multiplication”; “$F$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360464 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1642353f-4507-5ad2-b44d-dbb363c5619b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451977} {:answer/id #uuid "31347593-efa9-5691-bf34-5c9e82544287" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1642353f-4507-5ad2-b44d-dbb363c5619b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451977} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9e0714e-ab87-54a6-b980-317d89af3e69" :answer-field/key "$H$ is closed under matrix addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f3c025e-9d30-5379-ad6e-48d7f