7592186451984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "def6526f-9c66-55e6-a22d-bf06f1db3449" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451984} :answer-field/id #uuid "84ad88e6-0fa6-549c-ad5a-de9683ad51df" :answer-field/key "$H$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10fb8ec2-9c2e-55ae-85b0-700b4fea54e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-94631" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $H=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$H$ is closed under matrix addition” is false. For example, if ${A}_{1}={A}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a matrix from $H.$ So, $H$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement “$H$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. For example, if $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $k=2,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =2\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a matrix from $H.$ So, $H$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$H$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is false, while statement “$H$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is true. $H$ is a *not* subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$H$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360465 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09540a12-93a1-56bb-83a7-26a8ee5238bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451985} {:answer/id #uuid "cb44a1ec-0c76-5e3a-9081-665a0f335bf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09540a12-93a1-56bb-83a7-26a8ee5238bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451985} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fd29b5e-de2c-5d8c-8e1b-67530f61c337" :answer-field/key "$L$ is closed under function addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452840} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b89a6038-caa5-5b3b-b152-20edd8242a25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451987} {:answer/id #uuid "b228c6cd-02de-5f11-ae3b-e8df8795e61c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref