ous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $Q$ containing all polynomials of degree exactly $2.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$Q$ is closed under function addition” is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{2}$ and $g(x)=-{x}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nf(x)+g(x)={x}^{2}+(-{x}^{2})=0.\n$$\n\nSo, $Q$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement “$Q$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{2}$ and $k=0,$ then\n\n$$\nkf(x)=0\\cdot {x}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\n \nSo, $Q$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$Q$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$” is false, while statement “$Q$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$” is true. $Q$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$Q$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"} :activity/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574947} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575644}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360467 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb2