rue" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63d370e5-07ba-54c6-84b2-d2152f843127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452005} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd8599eb-5b6c-5f72-9e7f-4c37a37b62cd" :answer-field/key "$C$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452850} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aca4493b-8547-5286-83fb-deaf509091f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452007} {:answer/id #uuid "a167ab0d-34f6-5000-8bef-7f7a8ae3ed10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a167ab0d-34f6-5000-8bef-7f7a8ae3ed10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452008} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aa85b89-bf70-5661-b433-3d5ffe0aa95a" :answer-field/key "$C$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0f62d508-5cf6-5993-b139-949d11db546e" :question/math-academy-id "q-94635" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $C$ containing all polynomials of degree exactly $3.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$C$ is closed under function addition” is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{3}$ and $g(x)=1-{x}^{3},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)+g(x) & ={x}^{3}+(1-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =({x}^{3}-{x}^{3})+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $C$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement “$C$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{3}$ and $k=0,$ then\n\n$$\nkf(x)=0\\cdot {x}^{3}=0.\n$$\n\n \nSo, $C$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$C$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$” is false, while statement “$C$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$” is true. $C$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$C$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"} :activity/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481565} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481710}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360468 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "991f2f73-ac23-5191-ab80-7de9efee7e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452009} {:answer/id #uuid "2ead1013-7e82-50d2-9ea0-c2b7d5a04066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ead1013-7e82-50d2-9ea0-c2b7d5a04066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452010} :answer-field/id #uuid "506cf49e-9f52-5299-8ed3-6ff8e24478db" :answer-field/key "$E$ is closed under function addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452852} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fed6d2ec-aee8-5542-8372-ae559f20b93f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452011} {:answer/id #uuid "c05c0c3e-d50a-5489-b880-65368c86a869" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c05c0c3e-d50a-5489-b880-65368c86a869" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452012} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b6ad786-f4e4-5537-b235-5beb1d76d0c8" :answer-field/key "$E$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e1613e4-3825-5163-955a-c508dc5a7424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452013} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a4d7ea-1e52-5939-b1ad-c82fa09897e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5a4d7ea-1e52-5939-b1ad-c82fa09897e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452014} :answer-field/id #uuid "860bab32-e063-5c7b-9daf-21735a207ce5" :answer-field/key "$E$ is a subspace of $C[-2,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452854} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "902ecaea-e103-52f1-8446-e92ffd5c7e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452015} {:answer/id #uuid "b5359c31-2887-5291-8d2f-9c2c74acea93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "902ecaea-e103-52f1-8446-e92ffd5c7e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452015} :answer-field/id #uuid "063b6651-61e1-5617-8f54-44670f58aa5b" :answer-field/key "$E$ is **not** a subspace of $C[-2,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "44096d11-ac2c-5302-8668-0431e5543e9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94642" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[-2,2]$ of all continuous functions $f:[-2,2]\\to R$ and its subset $E$ containing all even functions.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n*Hint: $f$ is even if $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x\\in [-2,2].$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$E$ is closed under function addition” is true. If $f(x),g(x)\\in E,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(-x) & =f(-x)+g(-x) \\\\  & =f(x)+g(x) \\\\  & =(f+g)(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $E$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement “$E$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is true. If $f(x)\\in E$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(-x) & =kf(-x) \\\\  & =kf(x) \\\\  & =(kf)(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$E$ is a subspace of $C[-2,2]$” is true, while statement “$E$ is **not** a subspace of $C[-2,2]$” is false. $E$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$E$ is closed under function addition”; “$E$ is closed under scalar multiplication”; “$E$ is a subspace of $C[-2,2]$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"} :activity/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493386} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494067} {:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050453 :topic/id #uuid "4a436386-bf41-55c7-b1d3-02adad8f3faf" :topic/math-academy-id 1907 :topic/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces"} :activity/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560356} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561099}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360469 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73a902ed-7491-5586-a972-d357f55a0986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452017} {:answer/id #uuid "e02d1c16-f579-53fa-a7d0-24fb41030a0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73a902ed-7491-5586-a972-d357f55a0986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452017} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf830ad1-3967-59b5-8125-48068d769bf7" :answer-field/key "The constant function $f(x)=1$ for all $x\\in R$ belongs to $N.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452856} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f9fc86f-cdfb-5892-81a6-1b0d9bc7eb9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452019} {:answer/id #uuid "e30cf1d6-9863-5658-be8b-c21ac4b2d15c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f9fc86f-cdfb-5892-81a6-1b0d9bc7eb9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452019} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d0d49b1-179c-5765-84f1-7b10b986b831" :answer-field/key "For any $f(t),g(t)\\in N,$ we have $f(t)-g(t)=g(t)-f(t).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23886679-356d-53bc-88ed-fee5a9a5549f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452021} {:answer/id #uuid "2e29665f-db3f-5174-adca-366e367ba005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e29665f-db3f-5174-adca-366e367ba005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452022} :answer-field/id #uuid "e539d322-ecc4-522f-b82d-d2e18147e866" :answer-field/key "The addition of functions in $N$ is commutative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ff3e8b0-9d12-58ec-aef1-61a782559716" :question/math-academy-id "q-94649" :question/problem "Let $N$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=0.$  Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement “The constant function $f(x)=1$ for all $x\\in R$ belongs to $N.$” is false. The set $N$ contains only functions that evaluate to zero at zero. However, the function defined by $f(x)=1$ for all $x\\in R$ satisfies $f(0)=1\\ne 0.$ So, $f\\notin N.$\n\n- Statement “For any $f(t),g(t)\\in N,$ we have $f(t)-g(t)=g(t)-f(t).$” is false. For example, consider functions $f(t)=2t$ and $g(t)=t$ in $N.$ Then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)-g(t) & =2t-t \\\\  & =t \\\\ g(t)-f(t) & =t-2t \\\\  & =-t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(t)-g(t)\\ne g(t)-f(t).$\n\n- Statement “The addition of functions in $N$ is commutative” is true. Indeed, for any functions $f(t),g(t)\\in N,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t)=g(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nsince the addition of functions is commutative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The addition of functions in $N$ is commutative” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"} :activity/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508380} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509026}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "109109e7-1c69-56cd-9b2e-c839c768d3cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452023} {:answer/id #uuid "edac93af-d167-569f-a0e3-5072a6fee483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edac93af-d167-569f-a0e3-5072a6fee483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452024} :answer-field/id #uuid "b642997b-3b81-5855-8836-d3b87e046226" :answer-field/key "The zero-polynomial belongs to $F.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452859} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca7bbf3b-be14-56ec-b1e4-11147c4bf70c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452025} {:answer/id #uuid "f10e7355-6abf-5461-9323-1738529d32f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f10e7355-6abf-5461-9323-1738529d32f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452026} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9edafdb-244a-5445-97a3-cffa0d55e2ba" :answer-field/key "For the zero polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in F,$ we have $p(x)+0=p(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c78337cc-3bc4-5bc3-9ab8-a2d47e6765be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452027} {:answer/id #uuid "12dfbd69-08c1-535f-bfb5-4830de06751e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c78337cc-3bc4-5bc3-9ab8-a2d47e6765be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452027} :answer-field/id #uuid "df579160-ca8f-5445-a24d-a55d4ac1e168" :answer-field/key "There are polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in F$ such that $p(x)+q(x)\\ne q(x)+p(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "998609c4-bfb7-5e7d-ad89-b03b40316ca2" :question/math-academy-id "q-94661" :question/problem "Let $F$ be the set of polynomials of the form $ax+b,$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The zero-polynomial belongs to $F.$” is true. Indeed, the zero-polynomial can be represented as\n\n$$\n0=0\\cdot x+0.\n$$\n\nHence, $0\\in F.$\n\n- Statement “For the zero polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in F,$ we have $p(x)+0=p(x).$” is true. Indeed, for the zero-polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in F,$ we have\n\n$$\np(x)+0=p(x)\n$$\n\nsince $0$ is the unique zero element in the set of all polynomials.\n\n- Statement “There are polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in F$ such that $p(x)+q(x)\\ne q(x)+p(x).$” is false. For any polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in F,$ we have that\n\n$$\np(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x)\n$$\n\nsince the addition of polynomials is commutative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The zero-polynomial belongs to $F.$”; “For the zero polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in F,$ we have $p(x)+0=p(x).$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "902db5be-70c1-5674-b997-99068ce5edfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452029} {:answer/id #uuid "814a1883-467d-5324-b6ef-116433356eb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "814a1883-467d-5324-b6ef-116433356eb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452030} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c08151d-a778-5873-a9ce-fddc4ab45b26" :answer-field/key "The constant polynomial $1$ belongs to $E.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452862} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7a65cf4-7f49-5de1-8fe2-89baa7786a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452031} {:answer/id #uuid "e089eec9-7866-5f1a-a19f-c3d7e6029a81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7a65cf4-7f49-5de1-8fe2-89baa7786a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452031} :answer-field/id #uuid "f698df9a-9c04-5d46-ad26-9bbf7397619f" :answer-field/key "For the constant polynomial $1$ and any $p(x)\\in E,$ we have $1+p(x)=p(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452863} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ecbe2c7-ade2-5481-b820-bfe9f428123f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452033} {:answer/id #uuid "3ff2aef1-031d-5390-a56e-ad3f1cd32bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ecbe2c7-ade2-5481-b820-bfe9f428123f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452033} :answer-field/id #uuid "b85432db-4f8a-59af-af6d-ee5723b311ce" :answer-field/key "There are polynomials $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in E$ such that $[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)$ $\\ne p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)].$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86d246c9-ffba-5c6c-b83e-58058d87e01e" :question/math-academy-id "q-94686" :question/problem "Let $E$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{2}+1,$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The constant polynomial $1$ belongs to $E.$” is true. Indeed, the constant polynomial $1$ can be represented as\n\n$$\n1=0\\cdot {x}^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nHence, $1\\in E.$\n\n- Statement “For the constant polynomial $1$ and any $p(x)\\in E,$ we have $1+p(x)=p(x).$” is false. For example, consider the polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}+1\\in E.$ Then, \n\n$$\n1+p(x)=1+{x}^{2}+1={x}^{2}+2\\ne p(x).\n$$\n\nThe zero-polynomial $0$ is the unique polynomial such that for any $p(x)\\in E$ we have $0+p(x)=p(x).$\n\n- Statement “There are polynomials $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in E$ such that $[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)$ $\\ne p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)].$” is false. For any polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in E,$ we have \n\n$$\n[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)=p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)],\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The constant polynomial $1$ belongs to $E.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360475 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc6bcc99-b3af-511c-91ae-c4f89185a51b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452035} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2702cc-0039-5cff-ab51-3043f6c2744c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f2702cc-0039-5cff-ab51-3043f6c2744c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452036} :answer-field/id #uuid "649a81e0-ac77-5ec9-ae54-66f470930379" :answer-field/key "For any $A\\in R,$ we have $1\\cdot A=A.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452865} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b185955a-71e1-5cda-8cd9-a2fd6aaac544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452037} {:answer/id #uuid "38bb6b6b-c279-54ab-994d-20b82f110997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b185955a-71e1-5cda-8cd9-a2fd6aaac544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452037} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac94e2aa-cdd1-5e7c-b142-37d6eab761ea" :answer-field/key "For any $A\\in R,$ we have $-1(-1\\cdot A)=-A.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452866} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bf0ebb4-415a-54f5-9321-bd974e7046ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452039} {:answer/id #uuid "36b27cb9-c8ff-51e8-ad54-c9c26a9e4d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36b27cb9-c8ff-51e8-ad54-c9c26a9e4d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452040} :answer-field/id #uuid "27b49265-285f-512b-aebb-320dd01bc0ad" :answer-field/key "For any $A\\in R$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d30a6a74-1882-58de-a0e8-caf74485928f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94700" :question/problem "Let $R$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “For any $A\\in R,$ we have $1\\cdot A=A.$” is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in R$ with real entries, we have\n\n$$\n1\\cdot {a}_{ij}={a}_{ij}\n$$\n\nand, hence,\n\n$$\n1\\cdot A=A.\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $A\\in R,$ we have $-1(-1\\cdot A)=-A.$” is false. For example, consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ from $R.$  Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1(-1\\cdot A) & =-1(-1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =-1(\\begin{bmatrix}(-1)\\cdot 1 & (-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 0 & (-1)\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =-1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(-1)\\cdot (-1) & (-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 0 & (-1)\\cdot (-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =A\\ne -A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statements “For any $A\\in R$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.$” is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in R,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta ){a}_{ij}=\\alpha {a}_{ij}+\\beta {a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “For any $A\\in R,$ we have $1\\cdot A=A.$”; “For any $A\\in R$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"} :activity/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426537} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426556}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1474a3e2-e736-5b19-b171-2993227de350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452041} {:answer/id #uuid "9b98079f-fe90-5caa-80dc-7270db379b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1474a3e2-e736-5b19-b171-2993227de350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452041} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b953735-6549-5e74-ab38-2ec79639a675" :answer-field/key "For any $p(x),q(x)\\in L,$ we have $2(p(x)+q(x))$ $=2p(x)$ $-2q(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452868} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86ec80e9-0df8-5cfd-835c-fd48ded2c328" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452043} {:answer/id #uuid "69a7ca61-3cc1-5e61-baf2-dce127884e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69a7ca61-3cc1-5e61-baf2-dce127884e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452044} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c2d98f2-45aa-5106-9dbe-0b4791dcbb31" :answer-field/key "For any $p(x)\\in L$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452869} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b9c42b9-1d20-519c-b18e-c231243717e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452045} {:answer/id #uuid "d0500db8-c267-5db0-b0d1-5a3a33dc76d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452046}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0500db8-c267-5db0-b0d1-5a3a33dc76d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452046} :answer-field/id #uuid "a50fa798-62df-5307-a327-7013e9729e7e" :answer-field/key "For any $p(x)\\in L,$ we have $1\\cdot p(x)=p(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0778fc80-bc7a-5da8-b455-9670cb2d5afb" :question/math-academy-id "q-94711" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the set of polynomials of the form $ax+b,$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “For any $p(x),q(x)\\in L,$ we have $2(p(x)+q(x))$ $=2p(x)$ $-2q(x).$” is false. For example, consider the polynomials $p(x)=x+1$ and $q(x)=x-1$ from $L.$ Then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(p(x)+q(x)) & =2(x+1+x-1) \\\\  & =2(2x) \\\\  & =4x \\\\ 2p(x)-2q(x) & =2(x+1)-2(x-1) \\\\  & =2x+2-2x+2 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $p(x)\\in L$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$” is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in L$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $p(x)\\in L,$ we have $1\\cdot p(x)=p(x).$” is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in L$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus,\n\n$$\n1\\cdot p(x)=p(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “For any $p(x)\\in L$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$”; “For any $p(x)\\in L,$ we have $1\\cdot p(x)=p(x).$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"} :activity/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481574} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481750}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360478 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd62d7df-1d3e-5dab-b939-b97d87035195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452047} {:answer/id #uuid "d107fb09-76a7-5171-93cf-06b1fd198e65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd62d7df-1d3e-5dab-b939-b97d87035195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452047} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9e9157a-abab-567b-bcdd-196042a00252" :answer-field/key "$2x\\in T.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452871} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd65aa3b-de16-52fa-b452-7e6806041ad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452049} {:answer/id #uuid "e05f5154-0168-511c-b16e-60381e73e48c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e05f5154-0168-511c-b16e-60381e73e48c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452050} :answer-field/id #uuid "a073394d-9013-5e1c-ae29-d7b1de7ebc10" :answer-field/key "The scalar multiplication of polynomials in $T$ is associative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452872} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "550f8bb7-32bc-59af-a373-74d049435bbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452051} {:answer/id #uuid "4a9097d3-cae0-5637-8117-2b0fbfe255ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a9097d3-cae0-5637-8117-2b0fbfe255ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452052} :answer-field/id #uuid "14dca0d8-f85e-55c6-8fbc-2cd1271ca040" :answer-field/key "For any $p(x)\\in T$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03514ad7-d8b6-5b82-8d41-07ae43d6027c" :question/math-academy-id "q-94723" :question/problem "Let $T$ be the set of polynomials of the form $ax+2,$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $2x\\in T.$ is false. The set $T$ contains only polynomials of the form $ax+2,$ where $a$ is a real coefficient. However, $2x$ is not a polynomial of this form. So, $2x\\notin T.$\n\n- Statement “The scalar multiplication of polynomials in $T$ is associative” is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in T$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta p(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )p(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $p(x)\\in T$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$” is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in T$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The scalar multiplication of polynomials in $T$ is associative”; “For any $p(x)\\in T$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6289ad34-2393-5f5f-b7f0-a1ab1a3916f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Quadratic Form Types Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048555 :topic/id #uuid "a95c2c28-8d05-5d82-baa9-f51e879c16c9" :topic/math-academy-id 3127 :topic/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "491282d8-087a-5b6a-872d-6b0a47d66b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469722} {:answer/id #uuid "06e9071d-b647-5c18-bb45-e68fcc570e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "491282d8-087a-5b6a-872d-6b0a47d66b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469722} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef7d7514-e7a3-5427-b315-a9a69bce3495" :answer-field/key "$R(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470473} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83d2a2f4-ca6f-5c88-a824-d7acfdea58ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469724} {:answer/id #uuid "95ece7a6-9e69-5e78-8957-46a3c4175115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95ece7a6-9e69-5e78-8957-46a3c4175115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469725} :answer-field/id #uuid "64c56b6b-2880-560b-9538-f33060b8721c" :answer-field/key "$S(x)={x}^{T}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470474} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5da7956-0eb9-5adb-bdb6-5c327d8b35b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469726} {:answer/id #uuid "91c1f39d-20a8-532f-b2ef-a41f48e42975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91c1f39d-20a8-532f-b2ef-a41f48e42975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469727} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4dd36d1-3aac-54c6-b8e2-1006ae8abc43" :answer-field/key "$T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "96ce050e-6292-5b2a-b7c7-0c1f7f51192d" :question/math-academy-id "q-94731" :question/problem "$$\n\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ By evaluating the following quadratic forms at $x$ **only,** determine which of them **cannot** be negative-definite.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A quadratic form $Q(x)$ is negative-definite if $Q(x)<0$ for all $x\\in {R}^{n}∖{0}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the quadratic forms by substituting $x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}:$\n\n- Quadratic form $R(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}$ *might* be negative-definite. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(x) & =(-1)^{2}-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =1-9 \\\\  & =-8<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Quadratic form $S(x)={x}^{T}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}x$ *cannot* be negative-definite since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(x) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =33>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Quadratic form $T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}$ *cannot* be negative-definite since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(x) & =(-1)^{2}+3(3)^{2} \\\\  & =1+27 \\\\  & =28>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $S(x)={x}^{T}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}x$; $T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360480 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6289ad34-2393-5f5f-b7f0-a1ab1a3916f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Quadratic Form Types Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048555 :topic/id #uuid "a95c2c28-8d05-5d82-baa9-f51e879c16c9" :topic/math-academy-id 3127 :topic/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "195d16b7-57d2-5a98-ad60-1a8888bb7b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469728} {:answer/id #uuid "4588d0a9-3d54-5976-bc71-51d75a7695f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "195d16b7-57d2-5a98-ad60-1a8888bb7b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469728} :answer-field/id #uuid "37ef1083-cbd3-5fa2-b49e-f0aa3bd44d3f" :answer-field/key "$R(x)={x}_{2}^{2}+7{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470476} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dba4d436-16f6-5071-b037-fe3017f476b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469730} {:answer/id #uuid "5afbfc12-a6d2-5021-8f8e-5141947c51a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5afbfc12-a6d2-5021-8f8e-5141947c51a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469731} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ad01140-9faf-5249-96a3-7f505c7b7804" :answer-field/key "$S(x)={x}^{T}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -9 \\\\ -9 & -2\\end{bmatrix}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470477} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7f022e9-09a5-5650-8334-9f2aff11f4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469732} {:answer/id #uuid "b36fdf26-1340-5fc8-be86-56dcbc4ad2c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b36fdf26-1340-5fc8-be86-56dcbc4ad2c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469733} :answer-field/id #uuid "4676be30-c32d-51b3-b92b-dc162406a163" :answer-field/key "$T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c28bdf3-28d7-5fd9-bd3d-116dde5b3b96" :question/math-academy-id "q-94734" :question/problem "$$\n\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $x=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.$ By evaluating the following quadratic forms at $x$ **only,** determine which of them **cannot** be positive-definite.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A quadratic form $Q(x)$ is positive-definite if $Q(x)>0$ for all $x\\in {R}^{n}∖{0}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the quadratic forms by substituting $x=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}:$\n\n- Quadratic form $R(x)={x}_{2}^{2}+7{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ *might* be positive-definite. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(x) & =(-6)^{2}+7\\cdot 0\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =36+0 \\\\  & =36>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Quadratic form $S(x)={x}^{T}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -9 \\\\ -9 & -2\\end{bmatrix}x$ *cannot* be positive-definite since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(x) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -9 \\\\ -9 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}54 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-72<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Quadratic form $T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ *cannot* be positive-definite since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(x) & ={0}^{2}-(-6)^{2}-3\\cdot 0\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =-36-0 \\\\  & =-36<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $S(x)={x}^{T}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -9 \\\\ -9 & -2\\end{bmatrix}x$; $T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360481 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8f234a5-4dca-51cc-a721-905e11b5b82b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452053} {:answer/id #uuid "33e8d3e1-6dc9-5ee9-afd6-dfe0ded71a57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33e8d3e1-6dc9-5ee9-afd6-dfe0ded71a57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452054} :answer-field/id #uuid "198d37d8-be1b-531b-8314-150367bf35ca" :answer-field/key "For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $\\alpha (\\beta p(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )p(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452874} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eddf19da-e86e-5b84-b879-a247fbaded12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452055} {:answer/id #uuid "7f53d4b9-bd2e-5bb2-a7c1-14d4c4800e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f53d4b9-bd2e-5bb2-a7c1-14d4c4800e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452056} :answer-field/id #uuid "9edc3624-5ad8-5ae7-88bb-cc220f58903d" :answer-field/key "Multiplication by $1$ does not change elements in $U.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452875} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75c4607c-aae6-53c5-ac66-e6c8e8bc7d67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452057} {:answer/id #uuid "a469bd7d-0083-5e69-820b-0b0b38f0e091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a469bd7d-0083-5e69-820b-0b0b38f0e091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452058} :answer-field/id #uuid "25039299-3d17-58e9-8f21-b6bed2fe81e1" :answer-field/key "For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aa6bb928-4008-5011-93e0-eb9181dde1e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-94741" :question/problem "Let $U$ be the set of functions of the form $p(x)=ax,$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $\\alpha (\\beta p(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )p(x).$” is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in U$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta p(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )p(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement “Multiplication by $1$ does not change elements in $U.$” is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in U$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus,\n\n$$\n1\\cdot p(x)=p(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$” is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in U$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $\\alpha (\\beta p(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )p(x).$”; “Multiplication by $1$ does not change elements in $U.$”; “For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6289ad34-2393-5f5f-b7f0-a1ab1a3916f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Quadratic Form Types Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048555 :topic/id #uuid "a95c2c28-8d05-5d82-baa9-f51e879c16c9" :topic/math-academy-id 3127 :topic/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ed9f53d-8f5a-5d51-9fe5-b5701dfd17d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452059} {:answer/id #uuid "ba149761-6f03-59d5-b0a6-561327764bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ed9f53d-8f5a-5d51-9fe5-b5701dfd17d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452059} :answer-field/id #uuid "943f3044-0061-5817-a4df-8dc03a7939e6" :answer-field/key "$R(x)=8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ is positive-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452877} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d04386a-bf21-5e45-9825-7bc717ea9952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452061} {:answer/id #uuid "b350b539-18ee-52b0-bf06-3473cf1e8fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b350b539-18ee-52b0-bf06-3473cf1e8fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452062} :answer-field/id #uuid "1504f3a0-fa56-5d2a-8097-b25f32f379f3" :answer-field/key "$S(x)={x}^{T}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}x$ is negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6da48a5-41d7-502e-b0c3-5047cccb111f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452063} {:answer/id #uuid "a640cd11-4a14-590a-9fa1-6e2e6e1f2e6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6da48a5-41d7-502e-b0c3-5047cccb111f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452063} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fc57d82-6dd3-56dd-bc98-4625624ce330" :answer-field/key "$T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}$ is indefinite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "08e6755d-cc77-5492-aef8-539543b12cc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-94744" :question/problem "Which of the following statements regarding quadratic forms are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that, a quadratic form $Q(x)$ is:\n\n- positive-definite if $Q(x)>0$ for all $x\\in {R}^{n}∖{0};$\n\n- negative-definite if $Q(x)<0$ for all $x\\in {R}^{n}∖{0};$\n\n- indefinite if \n\n- $Q({x}_{1})>0$ for some ${x}_{1}\\in {R}^{n},$ and\n\n- $Q({x}_{2})<0$ for some ${x}_{2}\\in {R}^{n}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the quadratic forms in turn.\n\n- Statement “$R(x)=8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ is positive-definite” is false. Substituting ${x}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R({x}_{1}) & =8\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =8>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile substituting ${x}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R({x}_{2}) & =8\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-8<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the quadratic form is indefinite.\n\n- Statement “$S(x)={x}^{T}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}x$ is negative-definite” is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(x) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-2{x}_{1}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-(2{x}_{1}^{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2})<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in {R}^{n}∖{0}.$ So, the quadratic form is negative-definite.\n\n- Statement “$T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}$ is indefinite” is false. Indeed, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in {R}^{n}∖{0},$ the quadratic form is positive-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$S(x)={x}^{T}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}x$ is negative-definite” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360493 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124485 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "486cc512-416b-5eac-8964-1a87d533de72" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Given Set Is Linearly Independent Given Information on Its Elements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048257 :topic/id #uuid "8cc35c33-61af-5ac3-971b-a33b8bbdcb9d" :topic/math-academy-id 1908 :topic/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "394603d1-4814-5544-9172-11c68e08f316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452065} {:answer/id #uuid "7bda3b4f-9061-5a39-9045-d26cb78a9944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bda3b4f-9061-5a39-9045-d26cb78a9944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452066} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ffd1df2-f972-5161-a28f-449c584cfb74" :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452880} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "318ff92c-73e9-5ee0-aeee-1b2cedad0cd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452067} {:answer/id #uuid "ae733f27-a24e-5cc3-8aa6-a1078d7f759d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae733f27-a24e-5cc3-8aa6-a1078d7f759d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452068} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b957d62-15d8-5a0c-b43b-457d4dc9340a" :answer-field/key "${x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452881} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4e56851-d518-5ff4-9d71-1b336b27e4d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452069} {:answer/id #uuid "8b82d603-c5a1-5823-83d6-0e73228483f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4e56851-d518-5ff4-9d71-1b336b27e4d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452069} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfc426ed-bae3-552f-92fc-a3f6702bf682" :answer-field/key "$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is a linearly independent set" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452882}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0b4abe9a-af7a-5741-a378-7c07564b4cd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-94776" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that $\\{{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is linearly independent and ${v}_{1}=2{v}_{2}-{v}_{3}+{v}_{4},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}$” is true. Indeed, solving equation ${v}_{1}=2{v}_{2}-{v}_{3}+{v}_{4},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{v}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{v}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nThis means that ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$” is true. Since $\\{{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is linearly independent, we have that\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0.$\n\n- Statement “$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is a linearly independent set” is false. Since ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution, the set $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is a linearly dependent by definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}$”; “${x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048257 :topic/id #uuid "8cc35c33-61af-5ac3-971b-a33b8bbdcb9d" :topic/math-academy-id 1908 :topic/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces"} :activity/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436336} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436346}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124485 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "486cc512-416b-5eac-8964-1a87d533de72" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Given Set Is Linearly Independent Given Information on Its Elements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048257 :topic/id #uuid "8cc35c33-61af-5ac3-971b-a33b8bbdcb9d" :topic/math-academy-id 1908 :topic/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a21705a3-5a29-5f73-9072-c0a63af32911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452071} {:answer/id #uuid "3da1bd10-2484-51b1-9c33-1bb7f771c811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3da1bd10-2484-51b1-9c33-1bb7f771c811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452072} :answer-field/id #uuid "24c54d39-d8cb-5afc-8267-ab1e8cc75f8e" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452883} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1be81f08-17d0-5336-96ef-6bed2c7e7aa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452073} {:answer/id #uuid "cc44823a-b6fa-5661-989c-e371c7a18718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1be81f08-17d0-5336-96ef-6bed2c7e7aa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452073} :answer-field/id #uuid "930bab5e-8c86-58eb-a0d6-ec0c808c8686" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20dafd89-d5eb-572c-be39-5955d431ef9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452075} {:answer/id #uuid "706da707-f77b-5e37-b9f4-2828f578de41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "706da707-f77b-5e37-b9f4-2828f578de41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452076} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ac026ce-b6d8-5e03-9f40-19c298b1d5ba" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cbf9c53e-84bd-5e5c-95e0-1c3b39f57ad9" :question/math-academy-id "q-94779" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}({v}_{1}+{v}_{3})+{x}_{3}{v}_{2} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){v}_{1}+({x}_{1}+{x}_{3}){v}_{2}+{x}_{2}{v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+1\\cdot ({v}_{2}-{v}_{1})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}-{v}_{1})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Indeed, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0$ must have only the zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$  If this equation has a non-zero solution, $a\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}=0,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\na\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}+0\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent”; “${{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124485 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "486cc512-416b-5eac-8964-1a87d533de72" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Given Set Is Linearly Independent Given Information on Its Elements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048257 :topic/id #uuid "8cc35c33-61af-5ac3-971b-a33b8bbdcb9d" :topic/math-academy-id 1908 :topic/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eac94ca6-8049-5111-bc2a-d45e4fdc270b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452077} {:answer/id #uuid "c37d0316-ca6b-5c8e-8310-66a45ba19f96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eac94ca6-8049-5111-bc2a-d45e4fdc270b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452077} :answer-field/id #uuid "a63aee5d-829b-5d33-a17d-51582d4066df" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{3}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452886} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91df8c2f-9a86-530d-bd0c-56de10c94d19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452079} {:answer/id #uuid "599286cc-3c8f-59a0-93da-f7c7c1e6ae7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "599286cc-3c8f-59a0-93da-f7c7c1e6ae7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452080} :answer-field/id #uuid "55f26d78-2b79-501b-83ef-2c928e846e37" :answer-field/key "${2{v}_{1},{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8756b124-e725-5b72-83a2-827421bf6e79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452081} {:answer/id #uuid "ecbe3332-ad2a-5807-bec7-0421f2a405f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8756b124-e725-5b72-83a2-827421bf6e79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452081} :answer-field/id #uuid "21d0f96f-4afc-5e0e-8aeb-00020a2bc184" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "db8c1e1e-2555-50dd-bb83-7ef5667f1f43" :question/math-academy-id "q-94781" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{3}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+1\\cdot ({v}_{2}-{v}_{3})+1\\cdot ({v}_{3}-{v}_{1})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}-{v}_{3})+{x}_{3}({v}_{3}-{v}_{1})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{3}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “${2{v}_{1},{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{v}_{1})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2})+{x}_{3}(3{v}_{3}) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}_{1}){v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+(3{x}_{3}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{2{v}_{1},{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent” is false.  If ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0$ has a non-zero solution, $a\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}=0,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\na\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}+0\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${2{v}_{1},{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360498 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4105f1cb-eb48-5946-92f7-cd5e67689912" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type by Calculating the Corresponding Eigenvalues" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048555 :topic/id #uuid "a95c2c28-8d05-5d82-baa9-f51e879c16c9" :topic/math-academy-id 3127 :topic/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abae4a38-c5fd-5f02-a772-5aa129094bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469734} {:answer/id #uuid "61d28482-9aa5-5496-9fe2-e88afd3b2c83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abae4a38-c5fd-5f02-a772-5aa129094bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469734} :answer-field/id #uuid "1888ce5d-ffbd-5ed4-8be1-6bd4f78e3048" :answer-field/key "${x}^{T}\\,Qx,$ where the eigenvalues of $Q$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470479} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c36a82ef-f663-5517-a82d-dfb31295d4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469736} {:answer/id #uuid "1abaa9d3-1384-5eab-9d1f-4167841b8420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c36a82ef-f663-5517-a82d-dfb31295d4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469736} :answer-field/id #uuid "78bab090-2cec-52a7-8c1a-ea25848b4605" :answer-field/key "${x}^{T}\\,Rx,$ where the eigenvalues of $R$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-6$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=10$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470480} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8053ba89-f2f1-5607-8419-7cfe23f95b4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469738} {:answer/id #uuid "2a6d6721-833a-5366-b67a-9b57255478fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a6d6721-833a-5366-b67a-9b57255478fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469739} :answer-field/id #uuid "24fa5bdc-7dac-5793-b27a-1eadf77bbfa1" :answer-field/key "${x}^{T}\\,Sx,$ where the eigenvalues of $S$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=5$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a997acb-de91-5ebd-a6cc-103226757603" :question/math-academy-id "q-94787" :question/problem "Which of the following quadratic forms over ${R}^{2}$ are positive-definite?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a quadratic form $Q(x)={x}^{T}Ax,$ we have the following theorem:\n\n- $Q$ is positive-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are positive,\n\n- $Q$ is positive semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-negative (note that positive semi-definite quadratic forms include all positive-definite quadratic forms),\n\n- $Q$ is negative-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are negative,\n\n- $Q$ is negative semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-positive (note that negative semi-definite quadratic forms include all negative-definite quadratic forms), and\n\n- $Q$ is indefinite if and only if $A$ has both positive and negative eigenvalues.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our quadratic forms in turn.\n\n- Quadratic form “${x}^{T}\\,Qx,$ where the eigenvalues of $Q$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=3$” is *not* positive-definite since not all of the eigenvalues of $Q$ are positive (for example, ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ is not positive).\n\n- Quadratic form “${x}^{T}\\,Rx,$ where the eigenvalues of $R$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-6$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=10$” is *not* positive-definite since not all of the eigenvalues of $R$ are positive (${\\lambda }_{1}=-6$ is not positive).\n\n- Quadratic form “${x}^{T}\\,Sx,$ where the eigenvalues of $S$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=5$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=8$” is positive-definite. Indeed, all of the eigenvalues of $S$ are positive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${x}^{T}\\,Sx,$ where the eigenvalues of $S$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=5$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=8$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048555 :topic/id #uuid "a95c2c28-8d05-5d82-baa9-f51e879c16c9" :topic/math-academy-id 3127 :topic/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms"} :activity/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504030} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504717}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4105f1cb-eb48-5946-92f7-cd5e67689912" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type by Calculating the Corresponding Eigenvalues" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048555 :topic/id #uuid "a95c2c28-8d05-5d82-baa9-f51e879c16c9" :topic/math-academy-id 3127 :topic/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f98de070-157f-534d-80ca-0285e5ea31dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452083} {:answer/id #uuid "174de886-386b-5d7b-a04e-97378dcc50c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "174de886-386b-5d7b-a04e-97378dcc50c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452084} :answer-field/id #uuid "e799f149-b778-5e67-89e1-41f4feb99d40" :answer-field/key "The eigenvalues of $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452889} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4d1217-ff6e-508b-b3bc-dea5acc63146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452085} {:answer/id #uuid "78c882b5-c654-506d-9f34-f6de960b4eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78c882b5-c654-506d-9f34-f6de960b4eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452086} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb439c2a-82f5-579a-b442-b6cef060ee5e" :answer-field/key "${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dbe70c7-c5db-5456-9d9f-eceb402243d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452087} {:answer/id #uuid "7f3f8a7a-53c9-58ba-8c93-06d4c7b15b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dbe70c7-c5db-5456-9d9f-eceb402243d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452087} :answer-field/id #uuid "b68b3e83-f797-507a-a054-d24715a897e1" :answer-field/key "$A$ is indefinite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13d1d5cf-031d-5ebf-8e4c-d550f344afdd" :question/math-academy-id "q-94795" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a quadratic form $Q(x)={x}^{T}Ax,$ we have the following theorem:\n\n- $Q$ is positive-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are positive,\n\n- $Q$ is positive semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-negative (note that positive semi-definite quadratic forms include all positive-definite quadratic forms),\n\n- $Q$ is negative-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are negative,\n\n- $Q$ is negative semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-positive (note that negative semi-definite quadratic forms include all negative-definite quadratic forms), and\n\n- $Q$ is indefinite if and only if $A$ has both positive and negative eigenvalues.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “The eigenvalues of $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=5$” is true. Computing the characteristic equation of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +5 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =1,\\,5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite” is true, while statement “$A$ is indefinite” is false. Since all the eigenvalues of $A$ are positive, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is positive-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The eigenvalues of $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=5$”; “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048555 :topic/id #uuid "a95c2c28-8d05-5d82-baa9-f51e879c16c9" :topic/math-academy-id 3127 :topic/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e6b6069-a73e-55b4-8237-8d4f4f222dac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452089} {:answer/id #uuid "db8fa190-5652-57d4-9d6f-36a68e1d279f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db8fa190-5652-57d4-9d6f-36a68e1d279f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452090} :answer-field/id #uuid "88f61762-6f70-5d21-b1c1-800aae0f2fff" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=-3$ and $det(A)=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452892} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "311261b6-23c6-5a90-af11-2891a6bef398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452091} {:answer/id #uuid "3e682b91-127f-5abb-bc3a-e837723de4b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e682b91-127f-5abb-bc3a-e837723de4b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452092} :answer-field/id #uuid "4558c17e-723a-50fc-8a86-1acb9b4e8d09" :answer-field/key "${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bedbf47f-c0ac-5fc5-a3f5-ee511e9a5b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452093} {:answer/id #uuid "1a766f1d-8b11-5027-b338-059d385649a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a766f1d-8b11-5027-b338-059d385649a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452094} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdfd5bb3-65c5-50b4-abd6-2525ca2c0e80" :answer-field/key "$A$ is negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "81d008a7-fd35-5fff-9f9d-fc0e8e60bfec" :question/math-academy-id "q-94797" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=-3$ and $det(A)=2$” is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-3$ and \n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=2.\n$$\n\n- Statements “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite” and “$A$ is negative-definite” are true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-3<0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=2>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${a}_{11}=-3$ and $det(A)=2$”; “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite”; “$A$ is negative-definite”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360501 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048555 :topic/id #uuid "a95c2c28-8d05-5d82-baa9-f51e879c16c9" :topic/math-academy-id 3127 :topic/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7c44634-60fd-5951-9be7-dc5e18e58c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452095} {:answer/id #uuid "82947ba0-932e-5c2a-99e6-18adae0f5f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82947ba0-932e-5c2a-99e6-18adae0f5f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452096} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e7037ca-26f7-5e95-8a8e-f723accdd59c" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=6$ and $det(A)=17$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452895} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d96d178d-0a79-56c3-adbb-d837a0ce5c0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452097} {:answer/id #uuid "209120dd-a131-5d7f-a15d-2260c86df364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "209120dd-a131-5d7f-a15d-2260c86df364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452098} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3df2f8e-756f-5787-8a56-44336769a7ad" :answer-field/key "${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452896} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40074442-c36f-5a79-91a2-f79a296cd176" :ans