0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are positive-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${a}_{11}=6$ and $det(A)=17$”; “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048555 :topic/id #uuid "a95c2c28-8d05-5d82-baa9-f51e879c16c9" :topic/math-academy-id 3127 :topic/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "420ec396-a215-5051-bcb8-10ed9acc95ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452101} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c27e94-c52e-5c96-8d89-053964a8a2d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "420ec396-a215-5051-bcb8-10ed9acc95ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452101} :answer-field/id #uuid "83818ab7-8e39-5903-9ee3-959ef2554040" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=-5$ and $det(A)>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452898} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c441b03-7a1e-59f5-9515-8053ce5355d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452103} {:answer/id #uuid "cd8eaa01-f5f3-50e0-9b13-165b38fc8277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd8eaa01-f5f3-50e0-9b13-165b38fc8277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452104} :answer-field/id #uuid "82bbe034-c71c-5eb5-aefd-fd09fd107a27" :answer-field/key "${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452899} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "897837ee-7319-5a6c-a781-a2bf0d97f197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452105} {:answer/id #uuid "317ed741-0f0a-53c2-9948-7ac37ceef348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "317ed741-0f0a-53c2-9948-7ac37ceef348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452106} :answer-field/id #uuid "536fbf80-08b5-5e1a-a2ac-b0eae9c1cf2c" :answer-field/key "$A$ is negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "43115d1d-8694-5a95-b413-4600fbd2bc68" :question/math-academy-id "q-94804" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=-5$ and $det(A)>0$” is false. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-5$ but \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-8)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-8<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statements “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite” and “$A$ is negative-definite” are true. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-5<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|=1>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=-8<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite”; “$A$ is negative-definite” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048555 :topic/id #uuid "a95c2c28-8d05-5d82-baa9-f51e879c16c9" :topic/math-academy-id 3127 :topic/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms"} :activity/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504030} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504719}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360503 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048555 :topic/id #uuid "a95c2c28-8d05-5d82-baa9-f51e879c16c9" :topic/math-academy-id 3127 :topic/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e082f9d-d667-53bf-8ebe-ea0165b6dc26" :answer/typ