{:answer/id #uuid "f0fe63a9-b90e-5777-b826-3d8827fd649a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452111} :answer-field/id #uuid "42458164-cc6a-5528-9e47-6288386413d8" :answer-field/key "$A$ is negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7d5f731a-8eca-5400-88d7-dd10fc541120" :question/math-academy-id "q-94805" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=8$ and $det(A)<0$” is false. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=8$ but \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =21>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite” is true, while statement “$A$ is negative-definite” is false. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=8>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}|=7>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=21>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are positive-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048555 :topic/id #uuid "a95c2c28-8d05-5d82-baa9-f51e879c16c9" :topic/math-academy-id 3127 :topic/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms"} :activity/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504030} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504735}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbebdd1b-0716-55cb-8df6-12a35b517ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadratic Form Type Using Sylvester's Criterion" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048555 :topic/id #uuid "a95c2c28-8d05-5d82-baa9-f51e879c16c9" :topic/math-academy-id 3127 :topic/title "Positive-Definite and Negative-Definite Quadratic Forms"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fea1b93a-38ba-5c72-9bee-3fbe580f05cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452113} {:answer/id #uuid "81ba5de2-4ec0-55fe-bab8-33d6d9253f04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81ba5de2-4ec0-55fe-bab8-33d6d9253f04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452114} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f57c56b-b2e1-58e7-8141-026fa0dded98" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=-6$ and $det(A)<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452904} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85c12093-8dda-5103-9819-5b62a8cc94b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452115} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e0ca83-7bc5-54f5-b90f-2bcba9b76ad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85c12093-8dda-5103-9819-5b62a8cc94b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452115} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dc9ccf9-fe82-5943-aefd-c2e968dec187" :answer-field/key "${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452905} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c2dacb8-3a73-5142-9d28-821696fba02d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452117} {:answer/id #uuid "07437bee-0a6c-5947-bc81-ab31e28f0bc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07437bee-0a6c-5947-bc81-ab31e28f0bc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452118} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa4392f3-f738-5e5a-88d9-29ab52adafd4" :answer-field/key "$A$ is negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0bcde67-e6f1-5859-87e0-ff664264d2ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-94806" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=-6$ and $det(A)<0$” is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-6$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is positive-definite” is false, while statement “$A$ is negative-definite” is true. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-6<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}|=2>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=-6<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${a}_{11}=-6$ and $det(A)<0$”; “$A$ is negative-definite” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124592 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2588e089-4786-5346-b42d-65c2740ae2ab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Polynomial Vector Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048552 :topic/id #uuid "a92f5097-81a3-51a2-90e4-397763d967f0" :topic/math-academy-id 1909 :topic/title "Bases in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7a78d68-722c-5a86-b81e-827cf73ccb37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452119} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a1217b-b1b2-5202-a376-a348a355e361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8a1217b-b1b2-5202-a376-a348a355e361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452120} :answer-field/id #uuid "9515649f-9e44-5f61-baf3-729a68b97e8f" :answer-field/key "$\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{2}[t]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452907} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ef00e12-99c9-5c1c-9218-6b68325b5421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452121} {:answer/id #uuid "d6062610-898a-5fd9-8ec5-6314be543eb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ef00e12-99c9-5c1c-9218-6b68325b5421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452121} :answer-field/id #uuid "e447197c-21d9-5c73-8c22-d8a7a3296c07" :answer-field/key "${t}^{2}+1$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afe34d36-0fc3-563c-99d1-5708c805ab24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452123} {:answer/id #uuid "817f57a8-cd7f-5f80-806a-8559489f4936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afe34d36-0fc3-563c-99d1-5708c805ab24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452123} :answer-field/id #uuid "3906ed8a-b774-5d53-89da-c40c1ef74db1" :answer-field/key "$\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{2}[t]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac8aaff6-9636-552f-aae2-acac5b76a9ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-94842" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{2}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ over $R$ with degrees at most $2.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{2}[t]$” is true. Indeed, the equation \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot t+{x}_{2}\\cdot {t}^{2}=0,\n$$\n\n \nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ So, the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “${t}^{2}+1$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}$” is false. Notice that all linear combinations of\n\n$$\n\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}\n$$\n\nresult in polynomials without the constant term.\n\n- Statement “$\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{2}[t]$” is false. Indeed, the polynomial ${t}^{2}+1$ can't be written as a linear combination of the set  $\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$\\{t,{t}^{2}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{2}[t]$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360514 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124592 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2588e089-4786-5346-b42d-65c2740ae2ab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Polynomial Vector Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048552 :topic/id #uuid "a92f5097-81a3-51a2-90e4-397763d967f0" :topic/math-academy-id 1909 :topic/title "Bases in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87bb7a98-c575-525d-8f21-d662b93264ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452125} {:answer/id #uuid "f6638003-0464-5af5-afcf-6702ac0d7091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87bb7a98-c575-525d-8f21-d662b93264ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452125} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e9560bd-6ef4-547a-aa9e-0ec4d9c593f8" :answer-field/key "$\\{0,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{3}[t]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452910} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efcbc953-bb2d-59f8-9561-a8ac02a13abb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452127} {:answer/id #uuid "8374fd32-fbbf-5c22-85a2-c10487c1ebef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8374fd32-fbbf-5c22-85a2-c10487c1ebef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452128} :answer-field/id #uuid "37480e60-0e2c-59f9-b4be-acf090307d33" :answer-field/key "$3{t}^{2}-t$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{0,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f960d13-12c8-5bda-af69-0504f05800fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452129} {:answer/id #uuid "a61bf577-c31b-58b3-8d5f-774c53b573f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f960d13-12c8-5bda-af69-0504f05800fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452129} :answer-field/id #uuid "f82a5777-196c-533d-8aea-43409b51076b" :answer-field/key "$\\{0,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{3}[t]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8792da5-8116-548d-a9e9-a07944635528" :question/math-academy-id "q-94847" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{3}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ over $R$ with degrees at most $3.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$\\{0,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{3}[t]$” is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot t+0\\cdot {t}^{2}+0\\cdot {t}^{3}=0,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the first coefficient is nonzero, so the set is linearly dependent. In general, any set that contains a zero-vector is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “$3{t}^{2}-t$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{0,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$” is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n3{t}^{2}-t=0\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot t+3\\cdot {t}^{2}+0\\cdot {t}^{3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$\\{0,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{3}[t]$” is false. Since the set is not linearly independent, it can't form a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$3{t}^{2}-t$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{0,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360515 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124592 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2588e089-4786-5346-b42d-65c2740ae2ab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Polynomial Vector Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048552 :topic/id #uuid "a92f5097-81a3-51a2-90e4-397763d967f0" :topic/math-academy-id 1909 :topic/title "Bases in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17155733-9ce3-5dd6-84a2-3799b6de919b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452131} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcbd7ad-62b9-5a5a-ae56-b789911230aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfcbd7ad-62b9-5a5a-ae56-b789911230aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452132} :answer-field/id #uuid "98805a85-3b6d-5ca6-ada0-5674aa14b825" :answer-field/key "$\\{1,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{3}[t]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452913} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "032cab00-e88f-578f-82a6-78ad15f292ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452133} {:answer/id #uuid "bfaea224-86ea-5be7-81b2-96ffa8441385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfaea224-86ea-5be7-81b2-96ffa8441385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452134} :answer-field/id #uuid "64571fa1-9211-5a32-a07a-f6d759efd7bb" :answer-field/key "${t}^{3}-3t+8$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{1,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452914} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4a0b18d-16c0-524b-b6eb-f80d6f5f2adf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452135} {:answer/id #uuid "b48aff0a-c3a2-5b11-883a-17cbbaa86041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b48aff0a-c3a2-5b11-883a-17cbbaa86041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452136} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcb4e9fc-eea8-5d96-91cc-58151af98234" :answer-field/key "$\\{1,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{3}[t]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b873442b-9d2d-5d41-a7b6-d67882fe4b7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94848" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{3}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ over $R$ with degrees at most $3.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$\\{1,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{3}[t]$” is true. Indeed, the equation \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot 1+{x}_{2}\\cdot t+{x}_{3}\\cdot {t}^{2}+{x}_{4}\\cdot {t}^{3}=0,\n$$\n\n \nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0.$ So, the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “${t}^{3}-3t+8$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{1,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$” is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n{t}^{3}-3t+8=8\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot t+0\\cdot {t}^{2}+1\\cdot {t}^{3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$\\{1,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{3}[t]$” is true. Indeed, the set is linearly independent and for any polynomial in ${R}_{3}[t],$ we get \n\n$$\na{t}^{3}+b{t}^{2}+ct+d=d\\cdot 1+c\\cdot t+b\\cdot {t}^{2}+a\\cdot {t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$\\{1,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{3}[t]$”; “${t}^{3}-3t+8$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{1,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$”; “$\\{1,t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{3}[t]$”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360516 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124592 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2588e089-4786-5346-b42d-65c2740ae2ab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Polynomial Vector Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048552 :topic/id #uuid "a92f5097-81a3-51a2-90e4-397763d967f0" :topic/math-academy-id 1909 :topic/title "Bases in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1429c0a-89af-5805-8580-b73e7cd5d01a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452137} {:answer/id #uuid "624e0c32-5d2c-56d6-81a3-b8d4282b2eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1429c0a-89af-5805-8580-b73e7cd5d01a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452137} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e7b7fcb-d746-5098-8534-b43bcfff8673" :answer-field/key "$\\{0,{t}^{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{3}[t]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452916} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e3f86b7-428b-5f3c-96de-c85c2894