ments are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$\\{0,{t}^{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{3}[t]$” is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot {t}^{3}=0,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the first coefficient is nonzero, so the set is linearly dependent. In general, any set that contains a zero-vector is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “$-{t}^{3}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{0,{t}^{3}\\}$” is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n-{t}^{3}=0\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot {t}^{3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$\\{0,{t}^{3}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{3}[t]$” is false. Since the set is not linearly independent, it can't form a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$-{t}^{3}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{0,{t}^{3}\\}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360519 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124489 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "073042ee-d96d-5872-9681-ddcea43a2d37" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Matrix Vector Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048552 :topic/id #uuid "a92f5097-81a3-51a2-90e4-397763d967f0" :topic/math-academy-id 1909 :topic/title "Bases in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c0f5ce7-fdc1-5450-becc-3455d6e589d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452143} {:answer/id #uuid "9eaa2dd6-e820-58e5-8ff1-8304461c433e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9eaa2dd6-e820-58e5-8ff1-8304461c433e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452144} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9afc791-a8b1-53ee-ad26-58720715d425" :answer-field/key "${\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452919} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0fa1020-fa7b-566a-9214-2bd81560930f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452145} {:answer/id #uuid "b0aa9cd6-3ac4-5030-bdf4-5675f4a824c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0aa9cd6-3ac4-5030-bdf4-5675f4a824c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452146} :answer-field/id #uuid "71c4e941-084c-5fca-9534-f53207480cf7" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452920} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ec842c7-f3d8-5abd-9a36-6e857fae461a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452147} {:answer/id #uuid "33859395-8ac6-5662-ade7-d42fc98ae264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ec842c7-f3d8-5abd-9a36-6e857fae461a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452147} :answer-field/id #uuid "df7c3d55-f90b-5b9f-a9ed-d059376c3d11" :answer-field/key "${\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0064f075-2267-5e41-8556-443f519b3150" :question/math-academy-id "q-94859" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ So, the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}$” is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is false. For example, the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$ can't be written as a linear combination of \n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$\n\nsince all these linear combinations result in matrices with the entry ${a}_{12}=0:$\n\n$$\na\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+b\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2b\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$”; “$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360520 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124489 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "073042ee-d96d-5872-9681-ddcea43a2d37" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Sets of Vectors in a Matrix Vector Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048552 :topic/id #uuid "a92f5097-81a3-51a2-90e4-397763d967f0" :topic/math-academy-id 1909 :topic/title "Bases in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6975776c-3231-5fe9-a034-d001a5bd713d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452149} {:answer/id #uuid "103f259b-7946-5d48-b7f7-bcb24177d5ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "103f259b-7946-5d48-b7f7-bcb24177d5ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452150} :answer-field/id #uuid "830d65e4-5c68-5db2-b4bc-564b551c8f75" :answer-field/key "${\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452922} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uu