r-field/key "$A$ is an orthogonal projection matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452945}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e7f1c3f-c5ec-5613-8ec5-ead76a2389be" :question/math-academy-id "q-95339" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{10} & \\frac{3}{10} \\\\ \\frac{3}{10} & \\frac{1}{10}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $Q$ is an orthogonal projection matrix if and only if ${Q}^{2}=Q$ and ${Q}^{T}=Q.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement ${A}^{T}=A$ is true. Indeed, ${A}^{T}=A.$\n\n- Statement ${A}^{2}=A$ is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{10} & \\frac{3}{10} \\\\ \\frac{3}{10} & \\frac{1}{10}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{10} & \\frac{3}{10} \\\\ \\frac{3}{10} & \\frac{1}{10}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{100}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{100}\\begin{bmatrix}90 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{10} & \\frac{3}{10} \\\\ \\frac{3}{10} & \\frac{1}{10}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is an orthogonal projection matrix” is true since both statements ${A}^{T}=A$ and ${A}^{2}=A$ are true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${A}^{T}=A$; ${A}^{2}=A$; “$A$ is an orthogonal projection matrix”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360596 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133791 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e81030a-0151-5dea-b9bc-74aae2499482" :knowledge-point/title 