e mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $f$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X={5,10,15},$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y={12,13,14},$\n\n- the range of $f$ is ${12,13},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements “The codomain of $f$ is ${5,10,12,13,14,15}$” and “The range of $f$ is ${12,13,14}$” are false, while statement “The domain of $f$ is ${5,10,15}$” is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer “The domain of $f$ is ${5,10,15}$” only."}]
